  "brief": "Viatris is acquiring Pacira BioSciences for $1.65 billion as part of its push into the non-opioid pain market.\n\nViatris / Pacira BioSciences (Announced): Viatris to Acquire Pacira BioSciences. Viatris is acquiring Pacira BioSciences for $1.65 billion [2, 3, 4]. The deal is part of Viatris' push into the non-opioid pain market [2, 4, 6]. Pacira BioSciences is expected to become a leader in non-opioid pain therapies [6].\nAkzoNobel / Axalta (Pending approval): AkzoNobel and Axalta Deal. AkzoNobel and Axalta are a $25 billion deal [7, 8, 9]. The deal is pending EU antitrust approval [7, 8, 9]. No new information is available [7, 8, 9].\nWilliams / Momentum Midstream (Rumored): Williams to Buy Momentum Midstream. Williams is in talks to buy Momentum Midstream for $5.5 billion [10, 11]. Williams has agreed to buy Momentum Midstream [10, 11]. No further information is available [10, 11].\nCuraleaf / Aurora Cannabis (Announced): Curaleaf and Aurora Cannabis Deal. Curaleaf is acquiring Aurora Cannabis [12, 13, 14]. Curaleaf's takeover bid for Aurora Cannabis has been sweetened to $5 per share [16, 17, 18]. Curaleaf's offer for Aurora Cannabis has been improved [15, 18].\nMega Nova / SMC Electric (Announced): Mega Nova to Acquire SMC Electric. Mega Nova is acquiring SMC Electric [19]. Baker McKenzie is advising Mega Nova [19].\nSalt Creek Capital / MK Plastics (Announced): Salt Creek Capital Buys MK Plastics. Salt Creek Capital has acquired MK Plastics [20]. The deal was announced [20]. No further information is available [20].\nBarclays / McKesson (Announced): Barclays and McKesson Deal. Barclays is targeting McKesson's stock at $1,000.00 [21, 26]. McKesson and CD&R are close to a $5bn-plus deal to buy Option Care Health [24, 25]. McKesson and CD&R have agreed to acquire Option Care Health for $5.8 billion [26]. The deal was announced by McKesson [21, 22, 23].\nTradingView / Drilling Tools International (Terminated): TradingView Terminates Drilling Tools International Deal. TradingView has terminated its deal with Drilling Tools International [27, 28, 29]. The deal was terminated after the parties failed to reach an agreement [27, 28, 29]. The termination marks the end of the proposed acquisition [27, 28, 29].\n\nAlso worth knowing:\n- Alex Davis’ VC Firm Disruptive Targets $10 Billion for New Megafund [30].\n- OpenAI Leads Global AI Acquisition Spree: 195 Verified AI Mergers & Acquisitions Unveiled, Top Single Deal Hits $11 Billion Valuation [31].\n- Gorilla Technology Plans First US Data Center Deal, Targets Over 100MW AI Infrastructure [32].",
